**Fix the fail-fast key guard at lines 94-100. It never fires when both key variables are unset.**

If `ZAI_API_KEY` and `Z_AI_API_KEY` are both unset, line 95 assigns `undefined` to `process.env.ZAI_API_KEY`. Node coerces values assigned to `process.env` to strings, so the variable becomes the literal string `'undefined'`. The check at line 97 then compares against `undefined` and `''` and passes. The script skips the "refusing to run" exit. It dispatches a live run with a bogus key, and the failure then shows up as a "no verdict" or inconclusive result. That result misleads the operator about the cause. It also spends 5 s of wall clock plus the 5 s poll before it fails.

Resolve the key into a local variable. Validate it before you write it to `process.env`.

<details>
<summary>🐛 Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
-if (process.env.ZAI_API_KEY === undefined || process.env.ZAI_API_KEY === '') {
-  process.env.ZAI_API_KEY = process.env.Z_AI_API_KEY;
-}
-if (process.env.ZAI_API_KEY === undefined || process.env.ZAI_API_KEY === '') {
+const zaiKey = process.env.ZAI_API_KEY || process.env.Z_AI_API_KEY;
+if (zaiKey === undefined || zaiKey === '') {
   console.error('dd1-abort-spike: Z_AI_API_KEY is not set in the environment — refusing to run');
   process.exit(1);
 }
+process.env.ZAI_API_KEY = zaiKey;
```
</details>
